# Vibraxis — local environment template.
# Copy this file to `.env` (in the repo root) and fill in the value below.
#
#   PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#   bash:        cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored — never commit real keys. It is loaded automatically when
# the backend starts (npm run dev / npm run demo:smoke / backend start). A value
# exported in your shell overrides the one here.

# --- OpenAI API key ------------------------------------------------------------
# Enables the GPT-5.6 provider, i.e. the `gpt56-codex` route. Without it that
# route reports availability.gpt56=false; the `deterministic` route and
# `npm run demo:smoke` need no key at all.
# Get one at: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- GPT-5.6 model (optional) --------------------------------------------------
# Which GPT-5.6 model the `gpt56-codex` route requests. Must be a GPT-5.6 family
# id (starts with "gpt-5.6"); anything else is rejected at startup so the fixed
# "GPT-5.6 is the brain" provenance stays truthful. The id the API reports must
# equal this exactly (else gpt_model_mismatch) — so use a CONCRETE variant, not
# the bare "gpt-5.6" alias (which the API resolves to gpt-5.6-sol and would then
# fail the exact-match check).
#   gpt-5.6-sol   default / flagship (what the bare "gpt-5.6" alias resolves to)
#   gpt-5.6-luna  cheapest + fastest; plenty for the bounded intent step
# Unset => gpt-5.6-sol.
# GPT56_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna

# --- Backend port (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# Loopback port for the DJ Agent HTTP API; the Vite frontend proxies /api/agent
# to it. Defaults to 8787 when unset.
# AGENT_PORT=8787

# Codex CLI (the `codex-local` route) takes NO key here — it uses your locally
# logged-in Codex CLI. Nothing to set in this file for it.
